    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0243" n="227" xml:id="pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.248/8–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bruce</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-22T18:00:00-03:00">August 22, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1044. For Lovett. Although outstanding instructions prohibit sale US tactical
                    aircraft Argentina, British, Italian, Canadian tactical aircraft being sold
                    here. Representative North American Aviation states Argentina interested
                    purchase 66 overhauled surplus B–25 bombers. Our unilateral action is
                    ineffective and believe prejudicial US interest. My understanding in Washington
                    was ban had been lifted subject limitations military regulations governing sale
                    aircraft. Please advise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
